#problem([Generating $S_n$])[
  Prove $S_n$ is generated by $(1 med a)$ and $(1 med 2 med dots.c med n)$ if and only if $gcd(a-1, n) = 1$.

  #meta[★★][generators of $S_n$, transitivity plus transposition][Spring 2008 G1, Winter 2003 A3]
]

#problem([Generators of $SL_2(ZZ)$])[
  Prove $SL_2(ZZ)$ is generated by $mat(delim: "(", 0, -1; 1, 0)$ and $mat(delim: "(", 1, 1; 0, 1)$. (Hint: think of the Euclidean algorithm.)

  #meta[★★][Euclidean algorithm as row reduction][Spring 2006 G2, Fall 2006 G3, Spring 2020 #6 (finite-field $SL_2$, related setting)]
]

#problem("Subgroups of $QQ$")[
  Prove that every finitely generated subgroup of $QQ$ is cyclic, that $QQ$ has no maximal subgroups, and that $QQ\/ZZ$ has exactly one subgroup of each finite order.

  #meta[★★][divisible groups, f.g. torsion-free rank 1][Winter 2005 A2, Fall 2008 G3, Fall 2005 Sec.1, Spring 2009 G2]
]

#problem([$"Aut"(ZZ\/n)$ and groups of order 6])[
  Compute $"Aut"(ZZ\/n)$. Show $"Aut"(ZZ\/2 times ZZ\/2) tilde.equiv S_3$, and use this to classify the groups of order $6$ by hand.

  #meta[★][automorphism groups, semidirect products][Spring 2012 #10, Fall 2006 G1, Winter 2002 A2, Fall 2013 #1, Spring 2015 #8, Spring 2008 G2]
