= Set 2: Category Theory and Groups

// These sit outside the qual chapters; the qual touches them lightly (Spring 2015 #1, #2; Spring 2011 #10),
// but they build the universal-property fluency those problems assume.

#problem("Epimorphisms in Grp")[
  Prove that epimorphisms in $bold("Grp")$ are surjective. By contrast, show that the inclusion $NN arrow.r.hook ZZ$ is an epimorphism in $bold("Mon")$.

  #meta[★★★][universal properties, constructing test maps out of $G$][Spring 2015 #1, Spring 2015 #2]
]

#problem("Free groups on finite sets")[
  Prove that if $F(A) tilde.equiv F(B)$ as groups, then $|A| = |B|$ for finite sets $A$ and $B$. (Hint: count homomorphisms to $ZZ\/2$.)

  #meta[★★][counting homomorphisms out of a free object][Fall 2016 #1, Spring 2017 #3, Winter 2005 A3]
]

#problem("Coproducts")[
  Show that $ZZ\/2 * ZZ\/2$ (the coproduct in $bold("Grp")$) is the infinite dihedral group. Then explain why the coproduct in $bold("Ab")$ is so different.

  #meta[★][free products, presentations][Spring 2015 #1, Fall 2016 #1, Spring 2020 #1]
]

#problem("Fibered products")[
  Describe fibered products in $bold("Set")$ and $bold("Grp")$, and show that the kernel of a homomorphism is one of them.

  #meta[★][limits as universal objects][Spring 2015 #2 (categorical flavor)]
]

#problem("Representable functors on groups")[
  Show that $"Hom"_(bold("Grp"))(ZZ, -)$ is naturally isomorphic to the forgetful functor. What represents the functor sending $G$ to its set of elements of order dividing $n$?

  #meta[★★][Yoneda, representability][Spring 2011 Problem 10]
]

#problem("Mono, epi, and isomorphism")[
  Find a category where a morphism is both mono and epi but not an isomorphism. Then prove that a morphism that is mono and split epi is an isomorphism.

  #meta[★][basic categorical morphism types][Spring 2011 Problem 10]
]

